		{
			dependencies: ["550D01E852BFE592"]
			description: [
				"I then asked this reliquerer if he had a relic that helped him mine. Surely that's something that only Technicians or Engineers have access to."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&c\"This lil' contraption is a rather simple but effective tool. It essentially acts as a reusable smart stick of dynamite. Just put a bit of gunpowder in it, point it at a patch of ground you don't like, then blam! Instant explosion. It's actually better than an actual explosion in a couple of ways, since it doesn't hurt the user and it doesn't blow up the stuff you actually want, like ores, so that you can harvest them at your own leisure. Though, there is the flaw that it doesn't deal any damage with the explosion itself, which led to me innovating one of my favourite creations to date.\"&r"
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "471939DE22B5426B"
			rewards: [{
				count: 128
				id: "1A78708496A8CEF5"
				item: "minecraft:gunpowder"
				type: "item"
			}]
			size: 0.9d
			tasks: [{
				id: "48BBC7D237937923"
				item: "reliquary:destruction_catalyst"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 2.1999999999999975d
			y: 11.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["081070F7CBF61207"]
			description: [
				"&c\"Ah, my lucky change. This coin is actually imbued with a decent amount of luck, and that's not just a vague claim! Riches and valuable experience just seem to find me a preferable owner ever since I created this relic. Fortunately, it has a way to deactivate the effect, as I would've pissed off quite a number of powerful people that just happen to have a lot of treasures on display in their chambers, haha.\"&r"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"\"I've seen this coin in the hands of many people though.\""
				""
				"&c\"Well... it's not unique, but it's certainly a relic!\"&r"
				""
				"\"You don't seem convincing.\""
			]
			entity_vis_size: 1.0f
			id: "0901394AD3A5FDAB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6124B6F0F9E2A86C"
